 ## Overview
-UrbanIR Inverse Rendering jointly optimizes a neural scene representation and lighting parameters from monocular video to recover physically plausible albedo, normals, semantics, and shadows. [S1] It solves the ill-posed nature of inverse rendering in urban environments by computing visibility via volume rendering transmittance rather than explicit geometry, ensuring consistency between the learned density field and shadow casting. [S1]
